<article class="env-lemma" id="0A7S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A7S">Lemma <span data-tag="0A7S">47.16.9</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m, \kappa )$ be a Noetherian local ring with normalized dualizing complex. Let $I \subset \mathfrak m$ be an ideal of finite length. Set $B = A/I$. Then there is a distinguished triangle </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \omega _ B^\bullet \to \omega _ A^\bullet \to \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(I, E)[0] \to \omega _ B^\bullet [1]  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(A)$ where $E$ is an injective hull of $\kappa $ and $\omega _ B^\bullet $ is a normalized dualizing complex for $B$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Use the short exact sequence $0 \to I \to A \to B \to 0$ and Lemmas <a href="/tag/0A7Q" data-tag="0A7Q">47.16.4</a> and <a href="/tag/0A7N" data-tag="0A7N">47.16.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>